WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.285
Build one complete fictional sample.

00:00:02.285 --> 00:00:06.856
Explain quantity multiplied by rate plus a listed separate cost.

00:00:06.856 --> 00:00:14.168
The example supplies three hours at forty dollars per hour and twenty dollars of separate cost.

00:00:14.168 --> 00:00:17.368
Three times forty is one hundred twenty.

00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:21.481
Add twenty for a one hundred forty-dollar training subtotal.

00:00:21.481 --> 00:00:29.708
Give a supported practice task: two hours at fifty dollars per hour and fifteen dollars of separate cost.

00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:32.450
Two times fifty is one hundred.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.649
Add fifteen for one hundred fifteen dollars.

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:37.477
Check both calculations independently.

00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:41.134
These are invented training figures, not price recommendations.

00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:44.790
Taxes, discounts and other costs are not supplied.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.446
Include labeled blank fields and a review checklist.

00:00:48.446 --> 00:00:53.017
The person must state the exclusions and explain the result.

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:57.130
A training subtotal is not an approved customer quote.
